    "chunk_text": "Fasting is also a practice commonly found in Christianity. It aligns with the goals of purification and spiritual strength found in their traditions. This spiritual practice is seen as a way to achieve physical and spiritual health. Jewish fasting practices, like those on Yom Kippur is considered as a central procedure for atonement and spiritual renewal. Yom Kippur refers to a 25-hour fast on the holiest day of the year. Jewish law prioritises health and forbids fasting if it endangers life. The practice of fasting itself is understood to have health benefits."
