    "md5": "58ac9e54ccfe59fd99253ab7d01fdd7b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1629,
    "chunk_text": "Governments refuse to grant doctors\u2019 demands and opt for a game of chicken, driving the GMOA to strike or threaten to do so, and eventually politicians and bureaucrats give in after causing untold suffering to patients. The current dispensation is no exception. It is moving along the same rut as its predecessors in handling strikes in the health sector and elsewhere. Thankfully, sanity prevailed at long last, and the government swallowed its pride and opted to have a discussion with the protesting doctors.\n\nIn the health sector, it is not the interests of patients that prevail. They are subjugated to those of health workers and politicians in power. Doctors are not without blame for this sorry state of affairs. They are accused of leveraging their trade union power to have their own way. But it defies comprehension why the Health Ministry cannot handle a matter like doctors\u2019 transfers without creating issues that provoke the GMOA into protesting or even striking. The government must consult all stakeholders before carrying out transfers. Let it be urged to adopt a conciliatory approach instead of trying to bulldoze its way through. The fact that it has secured a supermajority does not mean it is free to act according to its whims and fancies. The JVP used its trade union might to facilitate its rise to power. Unnecessary battles with trade unions have the potential to be the undoing of the JVP-led government.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
