    "md5": "2dd1db42fcc1999aad29c0c672bb2196",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1931,
    "chunk_text": "Establishing courts, closing schools\n\nThe government has decided to establish four more high courts, which will be located in four houses formerly used as official residences of ministers, in Colombo 07, according to media reports. There is a need for more well-equipped courts, given the inordinate law\u2019s delays and the colossal backlog of cases that need to be cleared. There have been instances where some court cases dragged on for decades.\n\nAthauda Seneviratne, who served as a Minister of Justice, once revealed it had taken nearly 40 years for a case over a land dispute involving him to be concluded. In 2016, the Tangalle High Court sentenced four individuals to death over a murder that had been committed in 1989! By the time most child abuse cases are concluded, the victims are married with children. This may be one of the reasons why the victims of sexual violence choose to suffer in silence. The same goes for corruption cases; many culprits go the way of all flesh before being convicted. There are many other such cases pending at present. Unless remedial measures are adopted to ensure that justice is delivered expeditiously, the erosion of public faith in the judicial process is bound to take a turn for the worse.\n\nIt is joked that lawyers live on dates, and many a true word is spoken in jest. The law\u2019s delays are multifactorial in this country. What is needed is a multi-pronged strategy, but increasing the number of courts is surely a prerequisite for expeditious dispensation of justice.\n\nHowever, shouldn\u2019t institutions like courts be located away from residential areas for security and spatial reasons? There have been shooting incidents in and around courts. It has been revealed that underworld figure Keselbaddara Padme (Padmasiri Perera), who is currently being detained, planned to kill one of his rivals, Harak Kata (Nadun Wickremeratne), by attacking a prison bus with a claymore mine."
  },
