    "chunk_text": "The Ceylon Teachers\u2019 Union (CTU) is on the warpath, threatening a strike unless the government walks back its decision to go ahead with the proposed educational reforms. It says eight small schools have been closed in the North Central Province. CTU President Priyantha Fernando has said at a recent CTU event in Anuradhapura District that the incumbent government, which claims to espouse socialism, has done something that not even its predecessors described as agents of neoliberalism did. It says that as many as 1,500 small schools have been earmarked for closure, and downsizing the teacher service is one of the main conditions for a foreign loan amounting to USD 200 million. The government has not responded to this allegation.\n\nIronically, the self-styled Duishens and Altyanais in the JVP-led government are accused of devising ways and means of closing down remote schools instead of developing them to unleash their emancipating potential for the benefit of the poverty-stricken rural communities. Going by the JVP\u2019s rhetoric before last year\u2019s elections, one may have expected its activists to serve as volunteer teachers in underprivileged schools under an NPP government.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
