    "md5": "05c680129dafca3f2e4750d61b6066af",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1259,
    "chunk_text": "Rakuten Symphony and SLT-MOBITEL partner for open RAN trial in Sri Lanka\n\nRakuten Symphony and SLT-MOBITEL have signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) to deploy one of South Asia\u2019s first Open Radio Access Network (Open RAN) trials in Sri Lanka. The pilot project will build 4G and 5G sites using Rakuten Symphony\u2019s advanced Open RAN portfolio.\n\nThis initiative is a precursor to a potential nationwide deployment, aimed at enhancing SLT-MOBITEL\u2019s network agility, efficiency, and scalability. It is part of a broader strategic effort by Rakuten, supported by the Japanese government, to accelerate global Open RAN adoption and diversify the telecom supply chain.\n\nSharad Sriwastawa, President of Rakuten Symphony, stated the partnership will help SLT-MOBITEL achieve a lower total cost of ownership and faster time to market. Sudharshana Geeganage, Chief Operating Officer of Mobitel, said the trial demonstrates SLT-MOBITEL\u2019s commitment to next-generation technologies to support Sri Lanka\u2019s digital economy growth and deliver superior customer value.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
