    "chunk_size_bytes": 1759,
    "chunk_text": "The Weligama shooting was the 103rd of its kind to take place this year. 52 People have been killed in such incidents so far.  The 52nd victim Lasantha Wickramasekara  was a  native of Midigama in Weligama. He was earlier a member of the United National Party(UNP) but had split and aligned with the Sajith Premadasa -led Samagi Jana Balawegaya(SJB). Though Wickramasekara dabbled in open  politics, there was a darker side to his life too. He was allegedly linked to some  gangs engaged in drug peddling and possessed an unsavoury criminal record.Lasantha Wickramasekara alias Midigama Lasa was in that sense a \u201cDr.Jekyll and Mr.Hyde\u201d.\n\nLasantha\u2019s own life embodied a troubling duality, a politician with public appeal and electoral success, yet shadowed by a criminal past and former ties to the drug underworld; a \u201cDr Jekyll and Mr Hyde\u201d in Sri Lankan local politics.\n\nAccording to Police sources Lasantha Wickramasekara  alias Midigama Lasa was at one time closely associated with notorious drug dealer Nadun Chinthaka alias \u201cHarak  Kata\u201d. Lasantha  himself had  six cases  filed  against him in the Kurunegala,Matara and Galle Courts. He had received a suspended sentence in a case pertaining to a narcotics offence.Despite  this criminal record, the SJB had given Wickramasekara nomination for the Weligama Pradeshiya  Sabha elections in May 2025. It is said that Lasantha Wickramasekara had de-linked himself from gang activities and that there was a souring of relations with his erstwhile  underworld comrades.\n\nRival political parties especially the Janatha Vimukthi Peramuna(JVP)led National People\u2019s Power(NPP) had  criticized the SJB in general and Wickramasekara in particular over his  criminal record during the polls campaign."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2025-11-02-dbsjeyarajcom-66a76325",
    "num": "dbsjeyarajcom-66a76325",
    "date_str": "2025-11-02",
    "description": "Was the Killing of Weligama Pradeshiya Sabha Chairman  Lasantha Wickramasekara alias \u201cMidigama Lasa\u201d, a  Political Assassination or Gangland Execution?",
    "url_metadata": "https://dbsjeyaraj.com/dbsj/?p=86571",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dbsjeyarajcom",
    "time_ut": 1762097400.0,
    "chunk_id": "2025-11-02-dbsjeyarajcom-66a76325-0007",
    "chunk_index": 7,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "68ef5344657598792d583afb28bfc495",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2005,
    "chunk_text": "Rival political parties especially the Janatha Vimukthi Peramuna(JVP)led National People\u2019s Power(NPP) had  criticized the SJB in general and Wickramasekara in particular over his  criminal record during the polls campaign.\n\nThis led to much controversy.There were allegations of two NPP councillors being abducted.  It was later found to be a drama enacted against the SJB. There was another instance of shots being fired at the house of a PS councillor. A female councillor was threatened over the phone.After hectic politicking,the SJB gained control of the Weligama PS in July. Wickramasekara with 23 Votes was elected chairman. The NPP candidate got 22.\n\nThe Pradeshiya Sabha chairman\u2019s troubles were not over after victory. Lasantha  started getting  death threats from the time he was sworn in as Weligama PS Chairman. It appeared that the threats were from his erstwhile gangster comrades. It was indeed a puzzle as to why the \u201cgangsters\u201dchose to threaten him after becoming chairman instead of doing so earlier. Lasantha became a target of sorts. He was threatened openly through posts in social media.\n\nA desperate Wickramasekara wrote to the IGP in late August seeking Police protection. He submitted an affidavit titled \u201cRegarding  Securing my life Safety\u201d requesting appropriate security measures due to threats to his life.He was denied Police protection. Thereafter Wickramasekara went around with some unofficial bodyguards. However these bodyguards were unable to prevent him being killed.\n\nThe killing of the Weligama  PS chairman and the fact that he was denied Police protection was raised in Parliament.   SJB Leader and leader of the opposition Sajith Premadasa  stated as follows -\u201cHe(Wickramasekara) wrote directly to the IGP, warning of a planned assassination either while attending court or leaving the council premises. He submitted a sworn affidavit requesting adequate security during and after his official duties. Why did the government fail to protect him?\u201d"
  },
